      "text": "@andrewdfeldman @CulperResearch @cerebras Glad to see a direct response from $CBRS about the short report",
      "url": "https://x.com/aleabitoreddit/status/2118387249087918591",
      "time": "Thu Nov 05 16:57:32 +0000 2026",
      "cashtags": [
        "CBRS"
      ],
      "is_retweet": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Last week, a short seller, @CulperResearch, published a report arguing that @cerebras wafers wear out after about two years, and based on that premise the report suggested that the economics of our business are fundamentally challenged.  \n\nThat number is wrong, and given that the basis of the entire report is built upon that assumption, all of the assertions that follow are also wrong.\n\nWe do agree that the question of how long our systems last is a fair question, so we want to address the topic plainly.   \n\nIf you have a few minutes, I would encourage you to click on the link below, which wil",
      "url": "https://x.com/andrewdfeldman/status/2118344222558552167",
      "time": "Thu Nov 05 14:06:34 +0000 2026",
      "cashtags": [],
      "is_retweet": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Citadel in October: Tech companies created an AI bubble reminiscent of the dot-com crash.\n\nCitadel in November: “The setup has improved” \n\nEarnings continue to beat while AI infrastructure valuations compressed sharply.",
      "url": "https://x.com/aleabitoreddit/status/2118272043288547413",
      "time": "Thu Nov 05 09:19:45 +0000 2026",
      "cashtags": [],
      "is_retweet": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Why does it take some random anime character on X to push back against AI narratives?\n\nWhen you have all these companies worth billions, or even trillions, staying silent while their valuations crash.\n\nDepressed valuations does in fact trigger reflexive pressure on financing and counterparty confidence.",
      "url": "https://x.com/aleabitoreddit/status/2118262426101547280",
      "time": "Thu Nov 05 08:41:32 +0000 2026",
      "cashtags": [],
      "is_retweet": false
    },
    {
      "text": "@aleabitoreddit selloff so brutal it got serenity tryna save the AI space lol",
      "url": "https://x.com/rupakrt/status/2118259494161383882",
      "time": "Thu Nov 05 08:29:53 +0000 2026",
      "cashtags": [],
      "is_retweet": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Elon is the perfect example though, on what you should do to dispute the BS\n\nIf there’s a false WSJ report or X post on $TSLA or $SPCX… Even if it’s something as little as space datacenters won’t work, he just calls it out real time.\n\nI’m not saying every industry executive should do this, but at least hire a representative to defend against misleading narratives",
      "url": "https://x.com/aleabitoreddit/status/2118258090328162483",
      "time": "Thu Nov 05 08:24:18 +0000 2026",
      "cashtags": [
        "SPCX",
        "TSLA"
      ],
      "is_retweet": false
    },
    {
      "text": "I’m just calling out what I see with a failure in corporate communication, when so much is at stake.\n\nI’m really not sure why SK Hynix/Samsung representing SK’s economy let narratives of memory oversupply be dominated by their own customers on X.\n\nOr why $CBRS, which lost billions in valuation after the short seller report, is waiting for an analyst question in earnings to fix the damage \n\nOr why many of the “guppies” that would face a death in the Neocloud market aren’t actively fighting back against that claim here.\n\nA lot of narratives and claims originated and were distributed via X.\n\nEven",
      "url": "https://x.com/aleabitoreddit/status/2118253723244007677",
      "time": "Thu Nov 05 08:06:57 +0000 2026",
      "cashtags": [
        "CBRS"
      ],
      "is_retweet": false
    },
    {
      "text": "@aleabitoreddit 👏@elonmusk this has become a wild place.  Shit far outweighs information.",
      "url": "https://x.com/Dubbiosismo/status/2118249589274821093",
      "time": "Thu Nov 05 07:50:31 +0000 2026",
      "cashtags": [],
      "is_retweet": true
    },
    {
      "text": "@aleabitoreddit Do you think X has that much influence? 👀",
      "url": "https://x.com/ValueSpectre/status/2118247732662219010",
      "time": "Thu Nov 05 07:43:09 +0000 2026",
      "cashtags": [],
      "is_retweet": true
    },
    {
      "text": "I think this is the time for AI companies to appoint representatives on X.\n\nTo directly combat misleading AI narratives affecting ecosystem valuations and their financing ability.\n\nThe financial incentives to amplify overblown fears are enormous.\n\nBoth from well-capitalized executives who benefit from smaller competitors collapsing.\n\nAnd from firms aiming to profit off deleveraging the AI trade.\n\nIt shouldn’t take quarterly earnings to finally push back against false rumors of oversupply or buildout delays.",
      "url": "https://x.com/aleabitoreddit/status/2118247436733055110",
      "time": "Thu Nov 05 07:41:58 +0000 2026",
      "cashtags": [],
      "is_retweet": false
    },
    {
      "text": "That’s just blatantly false, there’s heavy industry doubts if MicroLED are even commercializable for CPO.\n\nAlso regarding $COHR on optical demand: “We continue to see no signs of attenuation in demand.”\n\nLaser demand is independently as strong as memory, and Coherent / Lumentum wouldn’t be signing $20B or $5B LTAs left and right.",
      "url": "https://x.com/aleabitoreddit/status/2118240089025413421",
      "time": "Thu Nov 05 07:12:46 +0000 2026",
      "cashtags": [
        "COHR"
      ],
      "is_retweet": false
    },
    {
      "text": "If you look at what Democrats are actually saying, it’s literally reasonable. \n\nThe “statewide moratorium” threats until more protections are in was already enacted under a republican governor. \n\nThe new “not in my backyard” type of DC measures voted in with the 10 states, only affects a tiny % of planned compute buildout but it’s being extrapolated for everything\n\nFears that Democrats are going to halt all DC development and end AI is just stupid.\n\nAnd this false narrative was being pushed by republicans (now amplified by short sellers) so they could get voted in again.\n\nHyperscaler AI DC bui",
      "url": "https://x.com/aleabitoreddit/status/2118209743709933703",
      "time": "Thu Nov 05 05:12:11 +0000 2026",
      "cashtags": [],
      "is_retweet": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Yes $AAOI had a massive InP substrate purchase order earlier, and I don’t believe all of that is going toward transceiver lasers that Rosenblatt modeled.\n\nI believe have the similar 60%+ GM UHP laser capabilities that $COHR $20B LTAs and $LITE $5B LTAs are primarily for.\n\nWhile having a MC of <$5B and we’ll see some announcements there later.\n\nAs for $SIVE, it’s mainly about qualifications given they have the capacity now with foundries + 100m laser expansion plan. \n\n$MRVL + $LITE gives it an extremely clear window of opportunity as well, alongside current laser bottlenecks for qualifying play",
